2949:## 13. Curriculum Assets & Flashcard Decks
2953:- **Source format 2 (23 November 2026):** A canonical Gymnasium source deck carries `schemaVersion: 2`, and every card names its understanding goals in `originGoalIds`. The contract is `contracts/memory-deck/v2/`; `python3 scripts/validate_schemas.py` validates every deck against it. `npm --prefix app run sync:memory-deck-origins` writes the field from the kept records of the active card-review ledgers, and `check:memory-deck-origins` verifies it. The memory-card review check fails when a card's field differs from its kept record. Never write an understanding goal into a deck by hand that the ledger does not hold.
2954:- **Card tags `goal:<id>`:** They remain on the Physics and Chemistry cards as a checked mirror of `originGoalIds`, because removing them changes the card fingerprints of the review ledgers. The field is authoritative; a tag that does not mirror it fails the review check. Removing the tags is an open point of issue #85.
2955:- **Packages:** The closed package deck schema (`contracts/curriculum-package/v1/card-deck.schema.json`) has no such field. The release-model compiler drops `schemaVersion` and `originGoalIds` on purpose, so published package contents stay byte-identical; a package carries the reviewed relation in `lanes.memoryCards.activeCardDecisions`. The ordinary subject export keeps the field.
